// Naive schedule: single worker, no decomposition.
//
// Landed cycle 262 (epic S5; TASK-0341.02.01.06). Every kernel runs on
// `host`; no cross-worker dataflow means no `transfer` directives. The
// result must be bit-identical to reference.bin.
//
// HOST-ONLY (single-worker) schedule, but RUNS ON ALL 7 TIER-1 BACKENDS
// (epic S7, TASK-0341.02.01.08): `workers = { host }` means
// `used_workers <= 1`, so every backend delegates this schedule to the
// SHARED single-worker emitter `render_single_worker_main` (which fully
// emits the `for..until` break). The multi-worker walkers' `break_cond`
// fail-loud guard is NEVER reached here — it fires only for a
// `partition=workers` schedule. A DISTRIBUTED convergence schedule (the
// COLLECTIVE all-reduce + broadcast break) remains out of reach: it
// inherits the 16-jacobi/distributed blockage plus the collective-break
// machinery — the remaining scope of epic S7.

schedule for "../prog.algo.nuc" {
    workers = { host };

    place load_input       on host;
    place save_output      on host;
    place jacobi5_or_seed  on host;
    place max_abs_acc      on host;
    place ident            on host;

    // No loop transforms.
    // No transfer directives — there are no cross-worker edges.
}
